alias ExitStatus = std::process::ExitStatus;
alias Inputs = std::process::Inputs;

public fn run(inputs: Inputs) -> status: ExitStatus pure doc "The normalization_tables entry, invoked as `normalization_tables_run DIR` with DIR naming, relative to the working directory, a directory holding the Unicode 17.0.0 character database files UnicodeData.txt and DerivedNormalizationProps.txt. It reads every code point's canonical combining class and canonical decomposition mapping from UnicodeData.txt, recursively expands each canonical decomposition to its full (non-Hangul) form, reads Full_Composition_Exclusion from DerivedNormalizationProps.txt, and builds the primary canonical composition pairs from UnicodeData.txt's raw (one-step) two-code-point canonical decompositions that are not excluded. Hangul syllables (AC00..D7A3) are left out of every table and are composed and decomposed arithmetically at run time instead. It prints the Whitefoot source of six public const tables to standard output, each a deduplicated two-stage block table (one entry per 256-code-point block naming which deduplicated block holds its bytes, then each distinct block's bytes once) or a flat lookup array addressed by a table's own id: CCC_BLOCK_INDEX and CCC_BLOCK_BYTES for the combining class; DECOMPOSITION_BLOCK_INDEX and DECOMPOSITION_BLOCK_IDS naming, per code point, an id into DECOMPOSITION_OFFSETS, DECOMPOSITION_LENGTHS and the shared DECOMPOSITION_VALUES array; and COMPOSITION_BLOCK_INDEX and COMPOSITION_BLOCK_IDS naming, per starter code point, an id into COMPOSITION_OFFSETS, COMPOSITION_COUNTS and the shared COMPOSITION_COMBINING and COMPOSITION_COMPOSED arrays. It exits 0 after printing, 1 when an argument is missing, and 2 when a file cannot be read.";
